shape theory.fractal : theory.coherence, theory.coherence.contact-is-shape, theory.emergence {
  type: theorem
  layer: 0
  """
// Theorem 7.1 (Fractal Coherence).
// The Laws of Coherence apply identically at every level of
// emergence. An emergent shape is a shape, and its persistence
// requires the same coherence conditions as any other shape.
// There is no structural distinction between "fundamental" and
// "emergent."
//
// Let D be emergent from A and B. D is a shape. All shapes must
// satisfy Laws 0-3. The contact between A and B is itself a shape
// and must satisfy Laws 0-3 independently. By induction on emergence
// layers, the laws apply at every level.
//
// This is not a separate requirement imposed on emergent shapes.
// It is a consequence of the fact that emergent shapes ARE shapes,
// and contact IS a shape. The recursion grounds at the axiom.
//
// Derives from: theory.coherence (laws apply to all shapes),
//               theory.coherence.contact-is-shape (contact is a shape),
//               theory.emergence (emergence produces shapes)
  """
}
